Feature: TC_12_STAFF - Scheme Selection BISS CRISS MSSM RCSM E2E Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Regression Pack for Scheme Selection - Add BISS, CRISS" (BISSAGL-5919, AT-TC-01 to 04,
  #           tmslinks BISSAGL-14880 / 14879 / 14877 / 14876)
  #           "Regression Pack for Scheme Selection - Add MSSM, RCSM" (BISSAGL-7582, AT-TC-01 to 05,
  #           tmslinks BISSAGL-14893 / 14889 / 14885 / 14891 / 14890)
  # Rewritten 15-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary (the wording the MAPS features run with). One end-to-end
  # scenario; # SECTION markers show where each legacy scenario starts.
  #
  # Purpose:
  #   - the BISS and CRISS cards show the right acronym and full name, their View Details dialogs open, they have toggles
  #   - selecting CRISS and Protein Aid Scheme and submitting changes the application and is recorded in the history
  #   - a selection abandoned with Back changes nothing
  #   - the MSSM and RCSM cards show the right full name and can be selected and deselected
  #   - selecting Eco and submitting changes the application
  #   - every scheme on an inactive herd reports a selection state
  #   Each submitted change is reset and the reset is checked, so herd J1400098 is left as it was found.
  #
  # Legacy coverage notes carried forward:
  #   - Selenium printed the selection states and the toggle checks instead of asserting them. Here the states are
  #     noted before a change and asserted after it (changed) and after the reset (back to the noted state).
  #   - BISSAGL-7582 AT-TC-04 and AT-TC-05 were the same clicks (Eco select, submit, reset); run once here.
  #   - BISSAGL-7582 AT-TC-02 (A1211644) and AT-TC-03 (P1461522) only opened the application (legacy notes: "How do we
  #     check for inactive farmer", "Need MSSM and RCSM disabled herd"). Kept as open-only sections.
  #   - BISSAGL-5919 AT-TC-01 to 03 took herds from the "Herds with Submission" query; the previous TC_12 already used
  #     J1400098 (the BISSAGL-7582 herd) for them, and that is kept.
  #
  # Test data (kept as literals, as in legacy):
  #   J1400098 / 2024 (the herd that is amended and reset), A1211644 / 2024, P1461522 / 2023, N1041714 / 2025 (inactive).
  #   Login agr4442 (BISS Co-ordination 1). Password: TD:Password from the TestData row of this test case.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps (Scheme selection and amendments, History)
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Background:
    Given the staff user is logged in to the BISS internal portal as "agr4442"

  @regression @staff @scheme-selection @e2e
  Scenario: AT-STAFF-SCHEME-E2E-01 - Staff verifies the scheme cards and amends the scheme selection

    # SECTION 1 : BISS and CRISS cards, details dialogs and toggles - BISSAGL-5919 AT-TC-01 (BISSAGL-14880)
    When the staff user amends the application for herd "J1400098" for scheme year "2024"
    Then the scheme cards should be presented as follows
      | position | acronym | title                                                          |
      | 1        | BISS    | Basic Income Support for Sustainability                        |
      | 2        | CRISS   | Complementary Redistributive Income Support for Sustainability |
    And the following scheme details dialogs should be readable
      | scheme | title                                                          |
      | BISS   | Basic Income Support for Sustainability                        |
      | CRISS  | Complementary Redistributive Income Support for Sustainability |
    And the following schemes should offer a selection toggle
      | BISS  |
      | CRISS |
    And the selection state should be readable for the following schemes
      | BISS               |
      | CRISS              |
      | Protein Aid Scheme |
    When the staff user notes the selection state of the following schemes
      | CRISS |
    And the staff user selects the following schemes
      | CRISS |
    And the staff user deselects the following schemes
      | CRISS |
    Then the following schemes should have their noted selection
      | CRISS |

    # SECTION 2 : Change CRISS and Protein Aid Scheme, submit, check the history, reset - BISSAGL-5919 AT-TC-02 (BISSAGL-14879)
    When the staff user amends the application for herd "J1400098" for scheme year "2024"
    And the staff user notes the selection state of the following schemes
      | CRISS              |
      | Protein Aid Scheme |
    And the staff user selects the following schemes
      | CRISS              |
      | Protein Aid Scheme |
    And the staff user submits the amendment and confirms
    Then the application history should record "Amendment Submitted" today
    When the staff user opens the "BISS Amendments" screen
    Then the following schemes should have the opposite selection
      | CRISS              |
      | Protein Aid Scheme |
    # Post-test reset
    When the staff user deselects the following schemes
      | CRISS              |
      | Protein Aid Scheme |
    And the staff user submits the amendment and confirms
    And the staff user amends the application for herd "J1400098" for scheme year "2024"
    Then the following schemes should have their noted selection
      | CRISS              |
      | Protein Aid Scheme |

    # SECTION 3 : Select Protein Aid Scheme, go on, then Back and deselect - nothing changes - BISSAGL-5919 AT-TC-03 (BISSAGL-14877)
    When the staff user selects the following schemes
      | Protein Aid Scheme |
    And the staff user proceeds to the next step
    And the staff user goes back and deselects the following schemes
      | Protein Aid Scheme |
    Then the following schemes should have their noted selection
      | Protein Aid Scheme |

    # SECTION 4 : MSSM and RCSM cards, select and deselect without submitting - BISSAGL-7582 AT-TC-01 (BISSAGL-14893)
